{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB08875 - MONDO_5005",
  "verbalization": "Cabozantinib is associated with Renal Cell Carcinoma (RCC) through multiple indirect pathways, as evidenced by its indication for RCC and its relationship with Axitinib and Tivozanib, both of which are indicated for RCC. The evidence suggests that Cabozantinib may exert a therapeutic effect on Clear Cell Renal Carcinoma through mechanisms that involve the inhibition of tyrosine kinase activity, a common target in RCC. This is supported by the presence of a direct indication for Cabozantinib in RCC and its downstream relationship with Axitinib, which is also indicated for RCC. The shared indication for Tivozanib and Axitinib in RCC further reinforces the possibility of a mechanistic link between Cabozantinib and Clear Cell Renal Carcinoma. The integrated evidence suggests that Cabozantinib may act through a kinase-inhibiting mechanism, potentially targeting pathways critical to RCC progression. The observed relationships imply a possible role for Cabozantinib in the treatment of Clear Cell Renal Carcinoma, though further validation through experimental studies is required to confirm the exact mechanism and therapeutic relevance.",
